{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22367 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Oncostemonol B may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of target relationships. This is supported by the shared final score of 0.6231 across three distinct paths, indicating a consistent level of confidence in the relationship. All three paths indicate that Oncostemonol B acts as a target for HCC1599, which in turn targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This suggests that Oncostemonol B may exert its biological effects through HCC1599, which is a known modulator of the polycomb group (PcG) proteins, including EZH2/SUZ12/EED. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforcing this relationship supports the hypothesis that Oncostemonol B may function as a modulator of the PcG complex, potentially through HCC1599. The evidence is consistent and complementary, highlighting a possible role for Oncostemonol B in regulating PcG activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism of action.",
